(5. Key Takeaways) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf
0 -14 Td
(1. Relational schema design relies on mathematical functional dependencies to prevent data redundancy.) Tj
0 -12 Td
(2. Primary keys enforce entity uniqueness; foreign keys guarantee referential integrity across parent-child tables.) Tj
0 -12 Td
(3. ACID properties are essential for mission-critical banking, transactional, and educational records.) Tj
0 -12 Td
(4. Indexes improve read query throughput but introduce overhead during write \(INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE\) operations.) Tj
0 -12 Td
